preConditionHook:
// A STEEPLY SLOPING MOVING AVERAGE: the EMA has risen by at least slopeAtr
// ATRs over the last slopeLookback bars (long), fallen by as much (short).
//
// Not Momentum, which compares the closing price with the close N bars
// ago: this compares the EMA with ITS OWN value N bars ago and adds a
// threshold, so it is smoother and fires on different bars. Kept apart from
// EmaFlat -- |slope| <= T and slope >= T are not each other's negation, so
// the per-placement negate toggle cannot produce one from the other.
//
// The source's 20-tick threshold is restated in ATRs: MinMove/PriceScale
// are unregistered and the engine exposes no tick size, the substitution
// CloseBeyondEma and PriorSessionLevelTest make. Brooks gives no number
// for 'steeply up' at all, so slopeAtr is an optimizer input. The source's
// priorSessionEndOffset (measure yesterday's slope, trade today) is
// dropped: a session-anchored offset for no stated benefit, and the slope
// is persistent enough that reading it on the current bar is the same
// information.
//
// MultiWalk's WFSafe_Xaverage, the function the EasyLanguage twin calls,
// ported unchanged from EmaGapBar (the EMA reference, which carries the full
// measurements). MEASURED, EL_XAverage_Probe.txt (@OJ 240min, chart starts
// 2007 and 2010):
//   * the wrapper is BIT-IDENTICAL to the plain XAverage built-in at a fixed
//     length -- (wf - xa) * 1e12 printed exactly 0.0000 on all 17,785 bars;
//   * the SEED is the PRICE on the study's first calculated bar
//     (ctx.CurrentBar() == 1), not a length-term simple average;
//   * the recurrence is x + sf*(p - x), ONE statement, never sf*p + (1-sf)*x:
//     the two separated on 67% of probed bars past 100. Do not re-associate;
//   * there is NO warm-up hole, so no bar-count guard returning 0 on the
//     CURRENT value;
//   * an EMA NEVER FORGETS ITS SEED -- it only decays at (1 - sf)^n, ~330
//     bars -- so Max Bars Back and the chart start are part of this rule's
//     specification.
// LENGTH CHANGE MEASURED 2026-09-17 (EL_XAverage_Lag_Probe.txt): the wrapper
// recomputes sf on the bar the length changes and carries its state, with no
// re-seed (reconstruction error 3.6e-15; the three rival hypotheses were off
// by 1.9 to 42 price units). emaLength MAY therefore be optimized in grids --
// the "pin emaLength" caveat is retired, and this mirror, which derives sf
// from the raw input every bar and carries emaVal, already behaves that way.
// Scratch below is declared in localVariables, not at hook scope: the
// generator only prefixes declared locals, so a hook-scope declaration is a
// redefinition when this rule is placed twice in one strategy.
emaSf = 2.0 / (emaLength + 1.0);
if (ctx.CurrentBar() == 1) {
    emaVal = close[0];
} else {
    emaVal = emaVal + emaSf * (close[0] - emaVal);
}
// WFSafe_AvgTrueRange: MultiWalk's ROLLING accumulator, ported from
// AtrProfitTarget (the reference, with the measurements). Seeded with a full
// sum on the first calculated bar or when the length changes, and updated
// thereafter as TWO statements -- EL evaluates S[1] + in - out left to right,
// and folding it to S += in - out rounds differently (@OJ 2015-02-20).
if (atrLength != (int)atrLookback) {
    atrSum = 0.0;
    for (int i = 0; i < (int)atrLookback; ++i) {
        double hi = high[i] > close[i + 1] ? high[i] : close[i + 1];
        double lo = low[i] < close[i + 1] ? low[i] : close[i + 1];
        atrSum += hi - lo;
    }
    atrLength = (int)atrLookback;
} else {
    const int out = (int)atrLookback;
    double hiIn = high[0] > close[1] ? high[0] : close[1];
    double loIn = low[0] < close[1] ? low[0] : close[1];
    double hiOut = high[out] > close[out + 1] ? high[out] : close[out + 1];
    double loOut = low[out] < close[out + 1] ? low[out] : close[out + 1];
    atrSum += hiIn - loIn;
    atrSum -= hiOut - loOut;
}
atr = atrSum / (int)atrLookback;
slopeBand = slopeAtr * atr;
// LAGGED EMA READS, MEASURED 2026-09-17 (EL_XAverage_Lag_Probe.txt): the
// function's own [k] history is bit for bit the value it printed k bars
// earlier -- the lag1 and lag5 columns were exactly 0 on every bar past the
// lag on both charts (9,664 + 8,157 and 9,659 + 8,152 bars) -- and BEFORE
// that history exists ([k] on bars 1..k) the read returns 0.0, not the seed
// and not a -1 sentinel. So the zero-initialized mirrored ring buffer below
// is EXACT, and the rule GUARDS its own first k bars on the bar counter
// instead of comparing against that zero.
// Depth slopeLookback + 1 so that lag 0 and lag slopeLookback both live in
// the buffer; at slopeLookback = 0 the read collapses to the current value,
// as EL's ema[0] does.
// Re-seeded if the depth ever changes, the way BarRangeAboveStd's
// mirrored history is.
emaDepth = (int)slopeLookback + 1;
if (emaDepth < 1) {
    emaDepth = 1;
}
if (emaHistory.size() != (std::size_t)emaDepth) {
    emaHistory.assign((std::size_t)emaDepth, 0.0);
    emaCursor = 0;
}
emaHistory[emaCursor] = emaVal;
emaLag = emaHistory[(emaCursor + emaHistory.size() - (std::size_t)((int)slopeLookback)) % emaHistory.size()];
emaCursor = (emaCursor + 1) % emaHistory.size();
// Deepest lagged read: ema[slopeLookback].
slopeReady = ctx.CurrentBar() > (int)slopeLookback;
